  "holdout_metric": null,
  "surprise": "766 at 8 loops (750/795/753) against 510's 764 (743/815/734): +2 (+7/-20/+19), keep by the rule, pure noise. The pre-registered 'tying is the deficit' reading is falsified: at 2 loops this model is the untied six-block topology (entry A1 A2 B1 B2 exit, 9,558,528 parameters, 590's count to the parameter) and it scored 739 (733/769/715) against 590's 792 and the tied incumbent's 752 (731/795/729), with per-sample dev accuracy at 2 loops down on every seed, 0.396/0.415/0.371 against 0.422/0.444/0.417. So six distinct blocks trained at random depths fit and generalize no better than four; what the untied control has and this model does not is one role per block (each block trained at one fixed depth, always followed by the same block) and cheaper deep retries (20 rounds against 12-14), not more weights. With 506 (untied first pass, -25) and 511 (wide, -18) this is the third way of spending the spare 3.2M that bought nothing at 8 loops, and the cheapest: compute, memory and speed per loop count were the incumbent's (1-loop sampling 171-240 samples/s, 8-loop 64-126; 8-loop eval 94/88/87 samples/s in 752/809/815 s; totals 3,948/4,111/4,008 s). What moved is the loop gap, and for the wrong reason: metric minus diag +27 (17/26/38; 510: +12 = 12/20/5; 511: +19), the largest of any run whose 2-loop diag did not collapse, per-sample 8-vs-2 gap 0.050/0.044/0.057 (510: 0.039/0.037/0.026). It is bought by the shallow pass getting worse, not the deep one better: per-sample dev accuracy at 8 loops is 0.446/0.459/0.427 against 510's 0.461/0.481/0.443 (-0.015/-0.022/-0.016), at 2 loops -0.026/-0.029/-0.046, and the theorems 8 loops add over 2 sit at lengths 7-9 (seed 2: +11/+9/+12 at lengths 7/8/9 and +2/+3/+1 at 10/11/12; seed 0: +5/+1/+7 and +1/+1/+1), ordinary theorems the weakened A-B pass misses and A-B-A-B recovers, not hard ones. 501 and 503 in a milder form: the gap grows when the shallow pass is handicapped. Coverage held while per-sample accuracy fell, 507's and 510's pattern again: pass@64 at 8 loops by length, seed 0, 116/114/387/101/24/6/2 at lengths 7-13 (510 seed 0: 104/114/389/106/24/5/1). Pretraining went the capacity way as in 506 and 511 and reached nothing: 3,345/3,656/3,435 steps (bench 0.96x; seed 1 got a fast pod), val loss at 2 loops 0.0755/0.0835/0.0840 against 0.0824/0.0894/0.0912, lower by 0.006-0.007 on every seed and the lowest mean of this loop after 505; val at 1 loop above 2 loops by 0.0075/0.0007/0.0010 (predicted +0.002 to +0.008, two seeds under), flat from 2 to 8 within 0.0011; held-out greedy after pretraining fell to 0.922/0.949/0.925 (510: 0.943/0.960/0.965). RL as predicted: rounds 12/14/13 (510: 13/14/12), RL solved 1,249/1,288/1,259 (510: 1,264/1,314/1,243), round-2 1-loop acceptance 0.336/0.395/0.416 (510: 0.231/0.410/0.292), last-round 0.615/0.627/0.707 (510: 0.671/0.667/0.634; predicted 0.60-0.74; reading (c), below 0.60 on two seeds, did not fire), ft_steps 299-402, late rounds 102-142 s, held-out greedy after RL 0.982/0.980/0.976 (510: 0.984/0.986/0.985). Retries: pooled crack rates 18.1/21.6/25.9, 19.2/20.3/22.0, 8.7/12.7/13.0% at 2/4/8 loops (510: 15.1/18.1/19.0, 20.0/23.8/24.9, 15.3/17.0/17.1), rounds 3+ 17.5/19.8/22.4, 18.8/18.5/20.1, 8.0/12.7/11.9; depth orders them more clearly on seed 0 than in any 510 seed, 4 and 8 tie on seed 2, whose 1-loop pass was the strongest (0.707) and whose failed set was therefore the hardest. Interpretation, not established: alternating pairs give the trunk two maps that must each serve as first pass, refiner and decoded output at both parities, so each pass is a weaker prover than the tied core's, the 2-loop forward is 590's topology but not 590's training, and the deep unroll does repair work the tied core did not need. Keep note: 441,472 parameters are left under the cap, so the spare-parameter direction is closed for this incumbent, and per-sample accuracy is lower at both depths; a later experiment that wants the headroom back should compare against 510 and 512 both. Next: the 792 gap now points at multi-role training or RL budget, not at sharing weights across positions. Retrying at 2 loops only to buy 590's round count (511's proposal) tests the budget reading; a loop distribution that rarely decodes the shallow passes (most batches at 6-8 loops, a few at 1-2 to keep the cheap discovery pass; 501 fixed everything at 8 and lost the discovery pass) tests whether a pair can learn a non-converged iteration once it is not also the one-pass prover. If deep loops keep adding only repair on lengths 7-9, the metric will not separate a looped model from an untied one and the loop question needs a harder pool.",
